WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
StarTropics, Tropical Adventure of Epic Dimensions.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:27.980
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.160
I'm Mike.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.360
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:39.780
In terms of, you know, best thing to have on you during an alien invasion, are you going for the yo-yo first?

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.060
Always. If I'm a pitcher, yeah.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.220
What else would you want?

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.360
What's another object that a pitcher would use other than a yo-yo?

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.400
Like a pitcher plant?

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.020
Like a pitcher, like a baseball pitcher.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:57.440
Oh, I mean, I would have said something along the lines of like, very fertile soil.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.200
Yeah, that too. If you were talking about the plant.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.840
Yeah. But I don't really know what else.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:08.180
What do you ask? Well, what's weird is that, well, because that's the main weapon of the game and it's also not something that he had ready.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.120
Like, it's something you have to acquire.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:19.260
That's true. I mean, I could, I sort of get the leap in logic where it's like, oh, he throws a baseball, but then the baseball's gone.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.260
So you need something that like you can throw that'll come back to you.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.920
Like I get where they were trying to go, but you know, I don't know if exactly translates.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.480
I guess what was he supposed to be doing?

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.380
Like he didn't even have any luggage on him.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.740
Was he like going on vacation?

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.920
I didn't really quite.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:48.020
Well, I have a question about that, Sean, because I was going to ask this and I don't think it's this, but the way that the game starts, you could argue that Star Tropics is one of those very popular isekais right now.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:56.880
Excuse me? And Izekai is where you get transported into the game, you know, you're from Earth and then you go into Jumanji.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.760
So this is Ready Player One?

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.600
Yeah. Well, it's like a whole genre now.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.520
It's got its own like Wikipedia page and everything.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.980
But like, we don't really know a lot about Mike before the game starts.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:16.320
And I guess he just like his uncle lived here, his alleged uncle.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.220
And so you could just assume that he lived here.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.920
But like, why does he start on what looked like a helicopter pad?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:26.740
Like, it does feel like we're missing some pretty important information about how he got here.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:40.100
Yeah. I think that first of all, the whole his name being Mike thing kind of threw me for a loop because I had just gotten done name myself or I guess it naming the save.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.380
Yeah. My own name.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.560
And then it's Mike. And I'm like, does Mike know the people that did this?

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.220
Like, did you do this to me, Mike?

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.800
And I have an even better story than that.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.700
I was playing on Nintendo Switch Online and with the NES package on there.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.620
And I named it because the character entry screen looks so much like the Legend of Zelda.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:08.380
I was trying to be a little cheeky and name myself Link just to see if like they would do anything about it.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:15.760
It still called you Mike. And it still called me Mike, but that freaked me out, Sean, because then I was like, wait a minute, is this like a Nintendo Switch Online thing where it knows my name?

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.640
Yeah, they're like, we know your name's Mike.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:18.540
That link, asshole.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.260
Right, right, right. So they just started calling me by my name.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:24.220
It was very like, there's a moment in Doki Doki literature.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.840
I was going to say it, but that could be a spoiler.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.900
It could be a spoiler, but come on, who's going to play that game if they haven't already?

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:35.720
That's true. That one listener who comments right now.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.440
Mmm, that's too bad.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.500
Yeah. And so reframing in a second, let's get away from Mike and the yo-yo.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.760
Star Tropics is a top down action adventure game for the NES.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:55.120
It is very often compared to the Legend of Zelda, but I think we're all going to say that it's not the Legend of Zelda pretty quickly as we get into it.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:06.040
It has its own like tropical, hence the Star Tropics vibe going on there and all of the islands and towns having named after Cola.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.060
I didn't figure this out until the end of the game.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:17.280
And so I'm very sorry to say this, but the villain of the game is a guy named Zoda.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:26.280
And I finally figured out that that was supposed to be soda in relation to the Cola naming convention of like the world and everything.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.260
So I thought that was kind of cute in the long run.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.560
Wow. I didn't put that together.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:37.560
But yeah, I thought that it was just trying to be cute with food names.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.920
But it only did the one food.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.860
Yeah. I mean, it caught the Cola thing.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.460
I mean, it's just like, it's trying to be...

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.100
Well, there's like Banan Girl.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.920
Oh, I don't remember Banan Girl.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.400
The sick daughter.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.460
Oh, yeah. I guess I never really thought of that as banana.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.160
I thought it was like Bernadette or something.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.560
It's like how in Dragon Ball Z, all the characters are named after vegetables.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.600
Yeah. Or clothing.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:15.140
I did appreciate that like, it was just interesting that they like were trying to go with this, like, this idea of what like Americans like.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.960
Where it's like Cola and, you know, baseball.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.120
Speedos. Fat uncles.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.520
And just like, it's just like, oh, this is what it's like to be American.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.780
Everyone has this experience.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:31.640
But honestly, it was just like, it was interesting because this feels like such a Japanese game.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.400
But like the setting feels like weirdly American, but also tropical.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:43.780
So like, you know, it's an interesting mix where you're like all on islands, but it's like, oh, this is like a regular American boy.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:53.040
But then it's also still like wizards and, you know, fortune tellers and monsters and just different for the NES.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.420
And it was developed by Nintendo.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:01.300
Nintendo R&D 3 and Locomotive Corporation developed the game together, published by Nintendo.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.260
Here's the interesting thing.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.680
Never came out in Japan.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:10.580
It was released in North America when we're recording in 1990 and later in Europe.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.400
But this game, even though it was made by Nintendo.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.000
We're recording in 2026, just by the way.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.420
Oh, yeah, that's a good point.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.140
We're not living in 1990.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.000
You didn't find a very, you didn't find the very first podcast.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.220
But we are the only video game podcast.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.100
True, true. Go on.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:35.200
No, I just think that that's like, it's, you know, the NES is having it's probably its biggest moment ever.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:43.760
When you think about the compilation games that we're going to be talking about that they've re-released like Super Mario Brothers and Duck Hunt and World Class Track Meet altogether.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:49.140
They had the four player adapter and we're making games for that.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.440
It just feels like right now is like the height of the NES.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:07:00.220
And then we're also getting this, you know, Christmas release of Star Tropics where it's like, you know, this is the big game for the holiday.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:07.000
And it's not a surprise that it kind of tries to borrow some things from Zelda while being its own thing here.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:15.100
And I just feel like, yes, I agree with the it's funny that the islands are cola and stuff like that.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:20.800
But the larger like little kid going out on and I guess we'll debate how young this guy is.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:30.600
But little kid going on an adventure that kind of goes over his head similar to down to the receiving of the yo-yo being the legend of Zelda.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.020
You know, it's dangerous to go alone.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:42.380
Take this like this does become a pretty big adventure from what starts a relatively small scale of just small little town enter dungeon.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:49.120
Like the first couple chapters don't necessarily give away like how big this game can get.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:08:01.720
Well, I mean, you do escalate to talking to animals and saving like and having that kind of interspecies communication pretty quickly.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:05.660
So, I mean, it's not it's not a crazy shift.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:10.680
Like once that happens, then aliens is kind of like a foregone conclusion.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.940
You think that it goes from talking dolphins to aliens just like that?

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:21.040
I mean, it's just not once you got talking dolphins, all bets are off is what I'm saying.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.880
Sure. I guess once you have a giant snake in a cave, all bets are off.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.940
Sure. Okay, I'm glad we're in agreement.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:31.880
So talking about Legend of Zelda, though, I don't know.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:40.320
I actually outside of the menu system looking alike and everything in the top down part of it, I think that these games are very different.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.300
Do you guys agree?

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:45.960
Um, in there are more different like it's not a complete Zelda clone.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.480
I think that there are tons of similarities and tons of differences.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:57.080
Like it's like they took chunks of Legend of Zelda and then build other stuff around it is what it feels like to me.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:05.460
I mean, the dungeons like very, very similar, but then have these mechanics that are completely never anywhere to be seen in like any Zelda game that I'm aware of.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:10.300
So it's just yeah, I think the answer is kind of both if that's not a cop out.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:15.480
Yeah, it borrows a lot of the visual language of Zelda, at least the first one.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:19.860
And then the gameplay itself is a completely different genre.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.780
I wouldn't even call this game action adventure.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:38.760
I would say that it's almost more of a puzzle game than I know that there are enemies that you fight, but everything else like between the grid based movement and just how you actually go forth within the game is much more like puzzly than anything.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:43.540
So, yeah, I think it's it's wearing it's definitely wearing a Zelda coat of paint, though.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:49.960
Yeah, I mean, even the like for the as far as the similarities like in the dungeons, I mean, the way that you fight.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:52.900
Yes, you have a yo-yo, but I mean, it's pretty much your sword.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:10:04.880
And if you have enough health, you have a turns into a projectile and there's like, you know, items to turn the lights on and there's different like clothes you can wear that give you different power ups and things like that.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.880
Like that all is like it feels like the DNA of Zelda.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:15.800
But yeah, like you said that the tile layout and like the actual platforming that's in this game gives it like a totally different feel.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.220
So it's like, I don't know.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.020
I do think it is.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.680
I wouldn't go as far to say like, oh, yeah, this isn't really like Zelda at all.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:23.580
Just kind of looks like it.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.440
I think it's very, very similar to Zelda.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.860
But like it's not just a straight clone.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.420
Like it has a lot of its own stuff, too.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:39.060
You play as Mike Jones, a teenager, Mike Jones, classic, who travels to visit his archaeologist uncle, Dr.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:47.960
Stephen Jones, and quickly get into a rescue mission by the town chief or mayor or whatever they call him in the game.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:54.740
And it escalates quickly into ancient tech sci-fi and ghost town and evil ruins.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:59.460
And I guess there's a larger mystery behind the disappearance of his uncle even.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:07.900
But does Mike Jones read as this deliberate teen hero like that you would see in a movie, an American movie specifically?

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:12.600
Or does he feel unusually plain for a Nintendo protagonist?

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.300
I mean, Link's pretty plain.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:21.840
You know, he's like a template for you to put yourself onto, to project your own personality onto.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.060
But he has the fantasy element going for him.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.200
He's not just like you.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:28.900
You know, I feel like Mike is very like, this is a human boy.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.180
And he doesn't have like, he doesn't have anything.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.380
Like you could say Mario, right?

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:39.540
Human man. But technically they Mushroom Kingdom-ified him and made him more than just a plumber from Brooklyn.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.600
Human Italian man.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:47.120
I guess, I guess in that sense, it seems intentional where it's like, yeah, he is.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:52.460
I mean, other than being like an ace pitcher, he is just like, oh, he's just like an every man.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:55.920
And you can like put, you can just say like, oh yeah, he's just like me.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.480
He's a kid growing up in the United States.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:00.140
Ace pitcher. Just like me.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:01.580
Yeah. Ace pitcher.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:07.360
Ace pitcher, you know, uncle who's a scientist on tropical islands, helicopter, private helicopter rides just like me.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:16.960
But like, yeah, there's not, he doesn't talk is what, you know, like a lot of these old JRPGs and stuff where like the protagonist doesn't talk.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:18.400
So you can be like, oh, he's me.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.020
Or like, I'm doing, I'm treating him like I would, the way I would behave in this game.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:32.560
Yes, you're right about that, that he kind of does have a link persona in that regard, that he doesn't, he's a silent protagonist who just accepts what's going to him.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:36.640
And I always wonder, are they just leaving without what he says?

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.200
Or is the whole rest of the world like, that was fucking weird.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:40.700
Guy didn't say a word to me.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:52.660
I think all video games with a silent protagonist are kind of like having you mentally self-insert what a conversation would be like, you know?

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.240
Yes, I agree with that take.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.500
And that's why Link will talk in the Legend of Zelda movie.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.700
Oh, he's going to be voiced by Chris Pratt, isn't he?

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:09.240
Why not? He could be both and then they save on money when they bring him the movies together for the Super Smash Brothers movie.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:16.360
How much does the story actually motivate you moment to moment versus like the gameplay?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.540
Like this is trying to tell a large story.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.320
Are you buying into that at all?

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:25.780
Or is it more like this is a fun game and I just want to keep exploring this world?

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:30.100
Yeah, there was, the story's pretty weak in this game.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.080
And there's a lot of like funny moments.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:38.220
Like the, like talking to your Rob in your ship.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:49.580
Uh, and then talking with the dolphin and then finding out that there's a, uh, that there's like a, an Amazonian place.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:54.080
Um, and talking to all of the shirtless mayors.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.220
Like that's fun. It's, it's cute.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:01.060
It's, it's like funny and has, has a sense of humor to it.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:08.960
But like at no point does this, like at least in the amount that I played, is there, is there much of like a high stakes plot happening?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.900
Yeah. I mean, it, with, it's not, I never like invested in it.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:21.740
Like I would be if I'm watching the Shawshank Redemption or something like that, where I'm like, oh wow, what a well-told story this is.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:31.960
But, but as far as adventure game, kind of like this, kind of, kind of gives me, and I, you know, it's funny to say this because it came after this, but like original Pokemon vibes.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.900
Where I'm not like, well, no one's writing home about the, the amazing story in Pokemon.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:39.540
But it was always enough to be like, oh, to make me feel like I'm on the adventure.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:45.380
Like that's, as much as I do love like a Final Fantasy where the, like I'm, I can like really think about like what's going on.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.540
Sometimes this is all I need.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.000
It's like the story is just being told through like, oh, I'm exploring the world.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.820
There's an environment and like it's pulling me along.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.260
But as far as like, am I driven by the story or am I driven by the gameplay?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.780
I think this game is like really designed.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:07.300
If this is their intention, designed very well around driving you forward without you having to even like really pay attention.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.380
Or like, you know, to the story itself.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:14.200
Like it usually is like, it's not an open world like Zelda where you have to figure out where to go.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:16.840
It, it corrals you to the next part of the story.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.860
Every time you have to kind of take it in chunks.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:20.900
So it's like, that's what drives me forward.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:24.800
But I appreciate that there's this little charm and I can feel like, oh, here's a little lived in world.

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:26.360
Yeah, exactly. There's charm.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:35.200
That's not to say that I think it's bad that there was that like I wasn't getting sucked into a really thoughtful story.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:40.240
Like I also prefer this to every other cookie cutter.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:53.000
Like whether it's a fantasy RPG or if it's the shmup where the alien race has invaded Earth and you're the only ship that can save it.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:55.600
Like it's like it's better than both of those.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:02.780
Give me weird sci-fi tropical goofballery over that every day.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:17.840
Yeah. And I wonder, you know, I, I, I wonder if there's, if this is kind of like a lost art of having like a world, your video game world, just be sort of told more through like you exploring, just talking to people.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:19.860
There's a quick text box here and there.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:25.600
And then like, so the story is kind of just told through like the gameplay in that sense.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.760
And it's not trying to be this big, heavy story.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:33.720
And I'm going back to Pokemon because that's what I remember falling in love with when I played Pokemon Red, like in 1997.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:39.800
But like now when I play a Pokemon game, it's like, oh, here's, here's eight minutes of cut scenes.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.440
Then you walk for, you walk for five minutes and eight more minutes of cut scenes.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.460
And like, we also didn't like make a really good story.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:51.580
Like Pokemon, I swear, like, like, I think I watched before I played it.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:57.020
I watched like a YouTube video of Legends Arceus whenever that one came out.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:03.740
And I was, I swear I was scrubbing through the whole video, just trying to land on a spot that wasn't a cut scene.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.240
Like, I'm just like, why?

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:07.200
Like, this isn't a good story.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:10.540
That happened to me with the most recent one too.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.900
Legends EA. It was like, I was like, oh, let me see what this game's like before I buy it.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:17.100
And somebody upload the entire game and it was just cut scenes.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:20.400
And not even like, not even cut scenes with dialogue and action.

