01:20:05.700 --> 01:20:11.640
I said it earlier in the episode, but I truly believe that Star Tropics is what people feared

01:20:11.640 --> 01:20:13.920
Zelda would be before Breath of the Wild.

01:20:14.120 --> 01:20:20.460
An incredibly linear experience where everything is so streamlined that the next place you approach

01:20:20.460 --> 01:20:23.400
or room in a dungeon is always forward progress.

01:20:23.700 --> 01:20:29.700
There's tons of set dressing to distract you, but everything is planned down to the dialogue.

01:20:29.700 --> 01:20:37.440
Somehow, even if that sounds scathing, none of that mattered during my time playing this game

01:20:37.440 --> 01:20:46.960
and any sort of, uh, flaws or qualms I might have with this game, it is impossible to deny

01:20:46.960 --> 01:20:51.340
that, uh, this is one of the great games on the NES.

01:20:51.880 --> 01:20:56.480
Uh, is it a little limited by, uh, the time that it was made?

01:20:56.480 --> 01:21:04.040
Yes, but in terms of other NES games we've played, few have had an adventure this grand.

01:21:04.040 --> 01:21:08.440
And I know that that's funny because we were talking about how this story is just kind of whatever.

01:21:08.620 --> 01:21:11.880
I don't really feel that the story is just whatever.

01:21:11.880 --> 01:21:15.040
I think that, uh, it's silly.

01:21:15.040 --> 01:21:16.000
It's pulpy.

01:21:16.260 --> 01:21:21.980
It's a chapter of the month style adventuring, but it is an adventure nevertheless.

01:21:21.980 --> 01:21:29.940
And I really enjoyed, uh, this journey both from, uh, the gameplay side, from the story side,

01:21:29.940 --> 01:21:33.420
and just seeing, like, what they would do next.

01:21:33.420 --> 01:21:40.960
Even if it is very linear, that provides a focused experience that creates a lot of memorable moments

01:21:40.960 --> 01:21:48.680
like, uh, the piano and figuring out the, uh, the Do, Re, Mi code in order to open up the next gate.

01:21:49.360 --> 01:21:56.940
There are certainly, uh, things in this game that, uh, bothered me at first that I even eventually,

01:21:57.140 --> 01:21:59.340
like, came around on, such as the movement.

01:21:59.340 --> 01:22:05.120
It was something that I thought was going to be, like, well, this might hold it off the list while I was playing.

01:22:05.280 --> 01:22:06.840
But in the end, it didn't matter.

01:22:06.840 --> 01:22:12.140
And I still made it all the way through this game, not in spite of it, but alongside it.

01:22:12.340 --> 01:22:15.600
So, for me, this is an obvious essential games list choice.

01:22:16.100 --> 01:22:19.840
Joe? I, I'll just come right out and say I completely agree.

01:22:20.100 --> 01:22:21.940
Uh, this, I, I love this game.

01:22:22.020 --> 01:22:23.640
I mean, yeah. Or are there flaws?

01:22:23.860 --> 01:22:26.120
I mean, there are flaws in some of my favorite games of all time.

01:22:26.220 --> 01:22:27.680
I mean, in all of my favorite games of all time.

01:22:27.920 --> 01:22:31.920
So, this, this, this is another game that was kind of made for me.

01:22:32.140 --> 01:22:37.180
The, the feeling of adventure, the feeling of progressing through this adventure was, you know, like,

01:22:37.360 --> 01:22:41.360
like, I love the, the fact that I can, like, I can say, like, yeah, I got to the underwater caves.

01:22:41.360 --> 01:22:47.060
Like, and it's like, that's just such a unique, starting this game, you don't know that there's this underwater cave section.

01:22:47.180 --> 01:22:49.820
That there's a, you know, piano puzzle area.

01:22:49.820 --> 01:22:52.420
That there's, you get swallowed by a whale at one point.

01:22:52.740 --> 01:22:56.420
Like, it just feels like you went on, like, a real grand adventure.

01:22:56.420 --> 01:23:03.320
And then on top of that, uh, you know, the, the linearity of it kind of lent to what it was designed around doing.

01:23:03.560 --> 01:23:08.640
And then the dungeons, I mean, I, I really started to enjoy the, the puzzle elements of the dungeon.

01:23:08.780 --> 01:23:15.920
The fact that it felt like platformy in a way that it's very hard for NES games to do in this top-down style.

01:23:16.380 --> 01:23:22.820
Um, and it, you know, it kind of had a good balance of, like, action, platform, and puzzle to me.

01:23:22.820 --> 01:23:25.300
I, I, I think this is, this is a great game.

01:23:25.340 --> 01:23:33.700
And honestly, and, you know, recency bias here, but, like, this, I, I'm kind of considering this when we do our, like, oh, what's your top 10 of the year?

01:23:33.840 --> 01:23:39.720
But, like, maybe even, uh, infiltrating my top 10 so far that we've played at all, uh, NES games.

01:23:39.880 --> 01:23:41.480
So, definitely, uh, essential.

01:23:41.940 --> 01:23:43.940
Sean? Yeah, great game.

01:23:45.980 --> 01:23:48.780
Um, it, it, it, it's reputation definitely preceded it.

01:23:48.780 --> 01:23:57.420
Um, so, uh, it really did have a high bar to, uh, to, to, to actually impress me.

01:23:57.500 --> 01:23:59.060
And I think that it still did.

01:24:00.540 --> 01:24:02.740
Um, I'm also voting it essential.

01:24:03.120 --> 01:24:06.480
