01:24:06.480 --> 01:24:20.380
Um, but also, like, it, the people that, that, that do have a problem with the, with, like, movement and, like, feel that is, like, a complaint to, to, to keep it out of their even, like, liked games.

01:24:20.880 --> 01:24:26.180
Like, that would need a ROM hack to change the way that it moves.

01:24:26.380 --> 01:24:27.520
It's like, I don't know.

01:24:27.720 --> 01:24:30.340
It feels like you're not actually playing the game anymore, man.

01:24:30.340 --> 01:24:34.700
Like, it's, it's just weird that that exists, uh, to, to me.

01:24:34.880 --> 01:24:39.620
Uh, I wanted to, I wanted to shout that out when, when we were talking about it in the episode.

01:24:39.620 --> 01:24:41.100
So, I just wanted to throw that in there.

01:24:41.260 --> 01:24:46.940
Uh, I have nothing new to add to that, to your, uh, to your breakdowns, though.

01:24:47.100 --> 01:24:52.020
It's, it's, uh, I do still think that the, the story is bullshit.

01:24:52.020 --> 01:25:00.340
But I think that there's enough going on, like, that it, it's, like, it's, it's still, like, a sequence of funny or fun things.

01:25:00.820 --> 01:25:03.220
And that's good enough for me, especially on the NES.

01:25:03.560 --> 01:25:06.620
So, uh, very enjoyable game.

01:25:07.020 --> 01:25:13.380
Sean, I'm glad you brought that up about the ROM hacks, too, because it's just something I've been thinking about in general with all of the ROM hacks that exist.

01:25:13.380 --> 01:25:22.440
Because there's, like, a lot of different categories of ROM hacks, and the ones that are in the improvement category are always so interesting.

01:25:22.580 --> 01:25:25.720
Because improvement is, like, such a statement.

01:25:26.140 --> 01:25:33.420
Oh, yeah. You know, like, like, it's, it's one thing to make a hack where, uh, you know, oh, instead of Simon Belmont, it's Mario, right?

01:25:33.560 --> 01:25:35.820
Like, that's, that's cute ROM hack idea.

01:25:36.040 --> 01:25:45.320
To call something an improvement that could drastically change the game, and I use this example on our Discord, so apologies for the people who, um, already heard it.

01:25:45.480 --> 01:25:50.520
But the, there is a Castlevania ROM hack that removes the knockback.

01:25:50.940 --> 01:26:05.080
And while I personally enjoy that, right, it makes the game significantly easier, uh, it makes it, uh, more fun for me because the later stages have, uh, flying Medusa heads that purposefully knock you into nothing.

01:26:05.080 --> 01:26:07.300
So that you, uh, automatically die.

01:26:08.000 --> 01:26:10.760
That is just not the developer intention.

01:26:11.100 --> 01:26:14.860
And if there wasn't knockback, they would have designed the levels differently, right?

01:26:14.980 --> 01:26:19.480
Yeah. They, they designed it with, like, knowing that those Medusa heads were doing that to you.

01:26:19.720 --> 01:26:24.360
So sometimes I question, uh, the intentions of the improvements.

01:26:24.780 --> 01:26:26.580
Yeah, it's like. As a statement.

01:26:26.580 --> 01:26:38.420
If you're going to mod out, like, your encumbrance in Skyrim, or if you're going to mod out, like, losing your souls on death in Dark Souls or something.

01:26:38.540 --> 01:26:40.360
Like, I'm not saying that these are things that people do.

01:26:40.400 --> 01:26:41.840
Maybe those mods exist.

01:26:41.840 --> 01:26:44.020
But it seems, like, akin to that.

01:26:44.160 --> 01:26:47.320
Like, you are just, you are removing a mechanic.

01:26:47.380 --> 01:26:48.480
Not so much.

01:26:48.540 --> 01:26:50.640
Yeah. Like, removing a disturbance.

01:26:51.460 --> 01:26:55.460
I'd even say it seems worse than, like, modding out your encumbrance in Skyrim.

01:26:55.560 --> 01:27:01.000
Because, like, it's so fundamental to the, to the core of this game.

01:27:01.160 --> 01:27:02.680
Where, like, there's just a fine line.

01:27:02.800 --> 01:27:09.960
Where, like, I, you know, I, I, I'm open to some ideas of these, like, quality of life improvements in ROMs.

01:27:09.960 --> 01:27:17.540
But, like, it's a very fine line between what's a quality of life improvement of, like, basically a developer mistake that should have been better.

01:27:17.820 --> 01:27:21.120
And what's just, you're just changing it to a different game.

01:27:21.260 --> 01:27:24.920
Like, this is not, the game is no longer designed around the way it plays anymore.

01:27:25.180 --> 01:27:28.900
And I think that's what, like, removing the, uh, the movement thing.

01:27:29.020 --> 01:27:33.840
Which, like, a movement thing that, like, you know, maybe, you know, it's just me.

01:27:33.960 --> 01:27:37.300
But, like, didn't really seem like too much of a factor on my end.

01:27:37.300 --> 01:27:40.400
Like, it was not like, oh, this is unplayable, like I thought it was going to be.

01:27:40.800 --> 01:27:43.520
So, yeah, I think that would, that would change way too much for me.

